### Definition: "authored work"

The authored work is everything in this repository **except**:

- `collections/` in its entirety, and
- any path that contains its own `LICENSE`, `LICENCE`, `COPYING`, or `NOTICE`
  file — those files govern their directories, and this license does not apply
  to them.

Paths currently carrying their own license include, without limitation:
`skills/attention-span/` (AGPL-3.0), `skills/archify/`,
`skills/bro/`, `skills/oil-motion/`, `skills/no-ai-slop/`,
`skills/ppt-master/`, `skills/vercel-deploy/`, `skills/whiteboard-diagrams/`,
`skills/last30days/scripts/lib/vendor/`, and every subdirectory of `collections/`
that carries a `LICENSE`.

The most significant carve-out is `skills/attention-span/`, which is licensed
under the **GNU Affero General Public License v3.0**. It is copyleft and cannot
be relicensed under the terms above by anyone who has already received it under
the AGPL. Its own `LICENSE` file governs it, and that is the correct
arrangement.

