## Part 2 — Third-party content

`collections/` holds 15,070 files vendored from external projects. **They are
not covered by Part 1** and remain under the terms of their upstream projects.
Each retains its own `LICENSE` file where one was supplied.

| Collection | Upstream | Terms |
|---|---|---|
| `academic-research-skills/` | `github.com/Imbad0202/academic-research-skills` | **CC BY-NC 4.0** — © 2026 Cheng-I Wu. Non-commercial; **incompatible with any permissive grant**, and excluded from Part 1. |
| `cybersecurity-skills/` | `github.com/mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills` | Apache-2.0 |
| `ecc-upstream/` | `github.com/apps/ecc-tools` | MIT |
| `financial-services/` | `github.com/anthropics/financial-services` | Apache-2.0 |
| `huggingface-skills/` | `github.com/huggingface/skills` | Apache-2.0 |
| `impeccable/` | `github.com/anthropics/skills` | Apache-2.0 |
| `kaggle-skills/` | Kaggle, official | Apache-2.0 |
| `open-code-review/` | `github.com/alibaba/open-code-review` | Apache-2.0 |
| `agentic-design-patterns/` | derived from Antonio Gulli's *Agentic Design Patterns* | **No license file present** — see below |
| `claude-agent-architectures/` | derived from Anthropic's `claude-cookbooks` | **No license file present** — see below |
| `enterprise-ops/` | unknown | **No license file present** — see below |
| `media-production/` | mixed; `diagrams/` ships MIT | **No top-level license**; subdirectories vary |
| `reference-architectures/` | unknown | **No license file present** — see below |
| `scientific-skills/` | mixed; most content Apache-2.0, `pacsomatic/` MIT | **No top-level license**; subdirectories vary |

### Unresolved — treat as all rights reserved

Four collections ship **no license file**: `agentic-design-patterns/`,
`claude-agent-architectures/`, `enterprise-ops/`, and `reference-architectures/`.
Two more — `media-production/` and `scientific-skills/` — have no top-level
license and carry only per-subdirectory files.

Under default copyright, no license means all rights reserved. **Do not
redistribute these paths, and do not treat them as covered by Part 1,** until
their terms are established and a `LICENSE` is added to each.

### Vendored dependencies

`skills/archify/node_modules/` contains 4,172 third-party dependency files
committed to version control. Each retains its own upstream license. This is a
packaging mistake, not a licensing statement: the directory should be installed
from a lockfile rather than committed, and it is excluded from Part 1.

---

## Part 3 — Contributions

Contributions to the authored work are accepted under the terms in Part 1.
Contributions to `collections/` are not accepted — those trees are synced from
upstream, and local edits will be overwritten on the next sync.